, SPIM3 (32 MHz) and both UARTEs are separate. Max is 4 SPI, or 2 I2C + 2 SPI + 2 UART at once.","USB 2.0 Full-Speed is device-only (no host).","No ROM bootloader. Most boards (Adafruit, Seeed XIAO, nice!nano) ship the Adafruit UF2 bootloader in flash, but a blank chip or bare module needs SWD.","VDDH accepts 2.5-5.5 V (USB VBUS or Li-ion directly). In that mode GPIO voltage comes from REG0, which defaults to 1.8 V; set UICR REGOUT0 for 3.3 V I/O.","The bare chip is aQFN73 only (0.5 mm pitch with inner rows, needs via-in-pad or fine-pitch PCB). Most hobby designs use a pre-certified module such as Raytac MDBT50Q or Ebyte E73-2G4M08S1C.","The QSPI XIP window is 128 MB; 16 MB is a conservative practical figure. Mainline MicroPython, CircuitPython and Arduino (Adafruit nRF52 core / Arduino mbed) all support it."],"sources":["https://docs.nordicsemi.com/bundle/ps_nrf52840/page/keyfeatures_html5.html","https://www.nordicsemi.com/Products/nRF52840","https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C190794.html","https://jlcpcb.com/partdetail/RAYTAC-MDBT50Q1MV2/C5118826","https://www.sparkfun.com/nordic-nrf52840-ble-module-mdbt50q-1mv2.html"],"boards":["adafruit-feather-nrf52840-express","arduino-nano-33-ble-rev2","nice-nano-v2","supermini-nrf52840","rak4631-wisblock","xiao-nrf52840","xiao-nrf52840-sense","nrf52840-dk"]}